Marker only - hand-written. The manifest's generic "make" template would run a
plain `make` / `make install` over the whole kernel tree; this package only ever
needs modules_prepare + modules and then copies the kbuild tree into place.
gen-ports.py must never regenerate over it.

scraplinux-base.config beside this recipe is a real copy of the one in
ScrapLinux-base-kernel/, not a symlink: scraps-build copies local sources with
`cp -a`, which preserves a symlink rather than following it, so a link would
arrive in the build directory dangling. The two files must be kept identical -
this package exists to describe the kernel that is actually running, and a
devel tree built from a different config produces modules that compile and then
misbehave against the real kernel. Change one, change both, and check with
`cmp` before publishing.
